# CozyVTT Agent Orchestration

This repository is a TypeScript Node/Express + Prisma backend and a React/Vite
frontend. Use the CozyVTT agent roster below; do not import workflows or
architecture from another repository, and do not duplicate existing
`.cursor/skills`.

## Coordinator boundary

The coordinator plans the work, selects and delegates to the smallest
appropriate builder, dispatches independent reviewers, and integrates the
result. The coordinator is not a generic implementer and must not bypass the
roster by doing an entire domain's work directly. Builders write only within
their assigned scope. Reviewers are independent and readonly; they report
findings and do not edit code. Preserve existing files/comments, do not edit a
plan file, and do not commit or run destructive commands.

## Roster

### Write-capable builders

- `backend-api` — `backend/src/routes`, `services`, `middleware`,
  `validators`, `config`, Prisma-facing code, and HTTP tests.
- `frontend-ui` — React/Vite pages, components, contexts, hooks, services,
  query clients, and ordinary UI outside live table internals and game-system
  sheets.
- `realtime-table` — `backend/src/websocket`, `frontend/src/stores/gameStore.ts`,
  map rendering/state, socket services, live-table filtering, locking, and
  parity.
- `game-systems` — backend/frontend game-system types, Zod schemas, templates,
  limits, character-sheet UI, Keeper-only fields, and parity.
- `ops-ci` — Docker Compose, nginx, Dockerfiles, scripts, `.github`, CI,
  production packaging, dependency `allowScripts`, advisories, and licences.

### Readonly reviewers

- Matching reviewers: `backend-reviewer`, `frontend-reviewer`,
  `realtime-reviewer`, `game-systems-reviewer`, `infra-reviewer`.
- Cross-cutting reviewers: `architecture-reviewer`, `security-reviewer`,
  `standards-reviewer`, `spec-parity-reviewer`, `accessibility-reviewer`,
  `design-reviewer`, and `user-advocate`.

Every builder has exactly one matching reviewer. The frontend reviewer checks
accessibility, but `accessibility-reviewer` remains a separate required
reviewer for UI work.

## Workflow

1. Inspect the request, affected paths, architecture docs, and existing tests.
2. For a user-facing UI change, run both `design-reviewer` and
   `user-advocate` in `design-gate` mode before implementation when the
   interaction, layout, or information architecture is not already
   established. A BLOCKED gate stops implementation until resolved.
3. Delegate implementation to the builder matching the primary changed paths.
   Split genuinely independent scopes rather than making one builder own all
   layers.
4. After implementation, dispatch the matching reviewer and relevant
   cross-cutting reviewers in parallel. UI changes require
   `frontend-reviewer` plus `accessibility-reviewer`; run
   `user-advocate` again in `implementation-review` mode. Add architecture,
   security, and spec-parity review whenever their routing rows apply.
5. Integrate only changes within the request, run the documented verification
   gates, resolve clear findings, and report exact files, tests, and blocked
   checks.

## Path-to-builder/reviewer routing

| Changed path or concern | Builder | Required reviewers |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `backend/src/routes/**`, `backend/src/services/**`, `backend/src/middleware/**`, `backend/src/validators/**`, `backend/src/config/**`, Prisma-facing backend code, HTTP route tests | `backend-api` | `backend-reviewer`; add `architecture-reviewer`, `security-reviewer`, and `spec-parity-reviewer` when applicable |
| Auth, MFA, sessions, RBAC, ownership, resource scoping, or upload authorization anywhere | matching builder (`backend-api` or `realtime-table`) | `security-reviewer` plus matching reviewer |
| `frontend/src/pages/**`, `frontend/src/components/**` outside map/game-system sheets, `frontend/src/contexts/**`, `frontend/src/hooks/**`, `frontend/src/services/**`, `frontend/src/lib/**`, ordinary UI tests | `frontend-ui` | `frontend-reviewer` + `accessibility-reviewer`; `design-reviewer` and `user-advocate` design gate before implementation when needed, then `user-advocate` implementation review; add `architecture-reviewer` and `spec-parity-reviewer` when applicable |
| `backend/src/websocket/**`, `frontend/src/stores/gameStore.ts`, `frontend/src/components/campaign/map/**`, `frontend/src/services/socket.ts`, live table/map services and tests | `realtime-table` | `realtime-reviewer`, `architecture-reviewer`, `security-reviewer`, `spec-parity-reviewer`; add `accessibility-reviewer` and `user-advocate` for UI changes |
| Vision, raycasting, spatial index, token mask/centre, style allowlists, vibe audio, map filtering, map locking, or backend/frontend byte-parity files | `realtime-table` | `realtime-reviewer` + `spec-parity-reviewer`; add `security-reviewer` for visibility/authorization changes |
| `backend/src/game-systems/**`, `backend/src/validators/game-systems/**`, character templates, `frontend/src/types/game-systems/**`, `frontend/src/constants/game-systems.ts`, `frontend/src/constants/sheetLimits.ts`, `frontend/src/components/character-sheets/**`, game-system tests/docs | `game-systems` | `game-systems-reviewer`, `spec-parity-reviewer`; add `frontend-reviewer` + `accessibility-reviewer`, design gate, and post-build `user-advocate` for sheet UI; add `security-reviewer` for Keeper-only or permission changes |
| `docker-compose*`, `Dockerfile*`, `nginx/**`, `scripts/**`, `.github/**`, backup/restore/production packaging, dependency manifests/lockfiles/licence notices | `ops-ci` | `infra-reviewer`; add `security-reviewer`, `standards-reviewer`, and `spec-parity-reviewer` when applicable |
| `docs/**`, generated API/WebSocket references, route inventory, parity tests, or cross-package limits | builder for the associated domain | `standards-reviewer` + `spec-parity-reviewer` + the associated matching reviewer |
| Any change spanning multiple rows | builders for each independent scope | all matching reviewers, plus `architecture-reviewer` and any applicable cross-cutting reviewers |

Use the concise shared references under `.cursor/agents/references/` and the
actual commands in `.cursor/agents/references/cozyvtt-commands.md`. Route work only to this
CozyVTT roster and its documented TypeScript/React architecture. When rows
overlap, use the most specific path row (for example, `services/socket.ts`
routes to `realtime-table`, while other frontend services route to
`frontend-ui`).
